From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: the system's storage as counted, without a 1 GB floor

Settings > Storage shows as "System" what the apps, media and files do not
account for, but at least 1 GB, a phone's system partition. On PW3 the system
image is 576 MiB and is counted in the total (frameworks/base 0020): the floor
would show more than there is. The value is shown as counted, and not below
zero.

--- a/src/com/android/settings/deviceinfo/storage/StorageItemPreferenceController.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/deviceinfo/storage/StorageItemPreferenceController.java
@@ -22,7 +22,6 @@
 import android.content.Intent;
 import android.content.res.TypedArray;
 import android.graphics.drawable.Drawable;
-import android.net.TrafficStats;
 import android.os.Bundle;
 import android.os.UserHandle;
 import android.os.storage.VolumeInfo;
@@ -284,7 +283,7 @@
                         - otherData.externalStats.appBytes;
             }
 
-            final long systemSize = Math.max(TrafficStats.GB_IN_BYTES, mUsedBytes - attributedSize);
+            final long systemSize = Math.max(0, mUsedBytes - attributedSize);
             mSystemPreference.setStorageSize(systemSize, mTotalSize);
         }
     }
